# Expected verdict class: skipped (reason no_trigger). shouldTriggerVerifier fires
# only on hard signals (currency / date / accounting-ref / percent / duration), so
# an answer without one skips extraction and the pipeline checks nothing. That is
# `skipped`, never `approved`: `approved` needs at least one checked claim, all of
# them verified (see approved-deterministic.jsonl for that path). The judge never
# runs here. The ids keep their original `approve_` prefix — they are stable ids
# and predate the `skipped` class; the file held `approved` expectations until
# verdicts became evidence-bound.
